==English==
===Etymology===
From {{L.}} ''[[sine#Latin|sine]]'' ("[[without]]") + ''[[die#Latin|die]]'', the {{abl}} {{singular}} of ''[[dies]]'' (meaning "[specific] [[day]]"). Literally meaning "[[without]] a [specific] [[day]]".
===Adverb===
'''[[sine#Latin|sine]] [[dies#Latin|die]]'''
# [[without]] [[specifying]] a [[date]] (for a [[future]] [[event]]); [[indefinitely]]

